            "widthMm": 48,
            "alt": "Mathematical diagram",
            "overlayOf": null,
            "transparent": false,
            "axes": null,
            "spec": {
              "sourcePage": 9,
              "sourceRegion": "Question 2c, bottom-left grid cell",
              "description": "Unshaded triangle pointing left, with upper sloping side labelled 0.5, right side labelled 1.2 and lower sloping side labelled 1.3; no right-angle marker.",
              "mathematics": "The longest labelled side is 1.3. Test 0.5² + 1.2² against 1.3² exactly. The source drawing is schematic and its apparent side proportions are retained.",
              "answerVisibility": "Only the three supplied side lengths are visible in the question."
            },
            "derived": false,
            "reviewStatus": "needs-review"
          }
        ],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Right-angled; $0.5^2+1.2^2=1.3^2=1.69$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}a^2+b^2&=0.5^2+1.2^2\\\\&=0.25+1.44\\\\&=1.69\\\\h^2&=1.3^2\\\\&=1.69\\end{align*}$$\nSince $a^2+b^2=h^2$, the triangle is right-angled.",
