            "derived": false,
            "reviewStatus": "needs-review"
          }
        ],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Right-angled; $\\left(\\frac{3}{10}\\right)^2+\\left(\\frac{2}{5}\\right)^2=\\left(\\frac12\\right)^2=\\frac14$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}a^2+b^2&=\\left(\\frac{3}{10}\\right)^2+\\left(\\frac25\\right)^2\\\\&=\\frac{9}{100}+\\frac{4}{25}\\\\&=\\frac{9}{100}+\\frac{16}{100}\\\\&=\\frac{25}{100}\\\\&=\\frac14\\\\h^2&=\\left(\\frac12\\right)^2\\\\&=\\frac14\\end{align*}$$\nSince $a^2+b^2=h^2$, the triangle is right-angled.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 62,
